            "review_title": "Review at Nha Hang Viet",
            "review_text": "palsks\nChennai (Madras), India224 contributions\n0\nEnjoyed lunch before getting into Ben Thanh Market\nDec 2017 • Family\nNhah Hang Viet is Vietnamese Cuisine restaurant located right opposite to Ben Thanh market in Ho-Chi-Min city. We wanted to have a light lunch before stepping into market on the 31st December. The restaurant looked new with attractive decorations to welcome 2018! The ambience was of high class. The waiters and waitresses were youngsters with cheers on their faces. The restaurant is part of Satra F&B group. It serves many Vietnamese delicacies, we were sticking to rice and chicken dishes. We ordered BBQ chicken with white rice and chicken chunks with yellow rice. We also ordered apple cedar based drinks – Gold and Berry. All food were very tasty. Each dish portion was just adequate for one person only. There were no napkins on the table. When we asked, waitress gave us wet tissue packets. Later we came to know the tissue packs were charged in the bill. It is a good fine dining Vietnamese food restaurant. Hope this and photos help.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 6, 2018",
