            "review_text": "Wingc633\nHong Kong, China2070 contributions\n0\nDelicious Vietnamese Food\nNov 2016 • Couples\nIt is located opposite to the Ben Thanh market.\nI went there after touring around the market, I felt hungry at that moment so I searched around and found it.\nThe restaurant was clean and tidy, moreover, it was spacious, the distance between seats was quite good. The waitresses/waiters there were friendly and helpful. The waitress explained to me in details about the the content of the cuisine when I asked.\nI ordered spring rolls, grilled beef, coconut palm heart salad and two drinks.\nAll of them were delicious, it was out of expectation!\nThe total amount of my bill was around 450,000 VND. \nI wanted to go again before I left HCM but eventually I could not spare my time. I shall visit there again.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 5, 2016",
